.SH NAME
ssoossh-ssh-login - Authenticate via OIDC and load a signed SSH certificate into the agent (or files).


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh ssh login [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates a fresh keypair, sends the public key to the ssoossh server, opens the browser for OIDC approval, and waits over SSE for the signed certificate. Used from ssh_config's \fBMatch exec\fR, or interactively before a session.

.PP
A certificate that is already loaded and still valid is reused rather than replaced, so one approval covers every connection until it expires. Pass --force to replace it with a new one.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	request a new certificate even if a valid one is already loaded

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--key-size\fP=0
	ssh key size (bits for rsa, curve for ecdsa; ignored for ed25519)

.PP
\fB--key-type\fP=""
	ssh key algorithm to generate: ed25519, ecdsa, or rsa (default depends on FIPS mode)

.PP
\fB--no-agent-forwarding\fP[=false]
	do not request permit-agent-forwarding extension

.PP
\fB--no-port-forwarding\fP[=false]
	do not request permit-port-forwarding extension

.PP
\fB--no-pty\fP[=false]
	do not request permit-pty extension

.PP
\fB--no-user-rc\fP[=false]
	do not request permit-user-rc extension

.PP
\fB--no-x11-forwarding\fP[=false]
	do not request permit-X11-forwarding extension


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to the ssoossh config file

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address including scheme (e.g. "https://example.com") assumes https if omited.

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


